  "blueprint_md": "# Automation blueprint: B2B customer onboarding\n\n## Process summary\n\n- **Description:** A new business customer goes from signed contract to active account in CRM and ERP.\n- **Owner:** Sales Operations\n- **Executions per month:** 60\n- **Steps:** 6\n- **Analysis:** <timestamp>, process version 1, rules scoring-v1, LLM ok (fake/fake-deterministic-v1)\n\n## Current state\n\n- **Monthly hours:** 35.50\n- **Monthly cost:** 852.00\n\n## Automation opportunities\n\nOrdered by monthly time. Suitability measures whether a step can be automated, not how much it is worth.\n\n| # | Step | Method | Human control | Decided by | Hours/month | Suitability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| 3 | Review signed contract | AI_CANDIDATE | RECOMMENDED | RULES | 10.00 | 28 |\n| 4 | Decide credit limit | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 8.00 | 0 |\n| 5 | Create customer in CRM and ERP | API_INTEGRATION | NONE | RULES | 7.00 | 80 |\n| 2 | Verify company registry and tax ID | RULE_BASED | NONE | RULES | 6.00 | 85 |\n\n- **Review signed contract:** unstructured digital input without required human judgement\n- **Decide credit limit:** Input is mixed and integration readiness is none.\n- **Create customer in CRM and ERP:** the systems involved expose a usable integration\n- **Verify company registry and tax ID:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n\n## Proposed architecture\n\n- Workflow engine that runs the steps in order, with retries and an audit log\n- Rules step in the workflow engine with explicit, versioned validation rules\n- API connectors to the systems already in use\n- Model-based extraction or classification behind a schema-validated contract\n- Automated draft with a person confirming the result\n- Human review queue: flagged items wait for a decision, which is logged\n- Orchestrate the automated steps from a single workflow engine with retries\n- Route low-confidence and flagged items to a human review queue\n\n## Business impact\n\nEvery economic figure below depends on the assumptions listed after it.\n\n- **Hours freed per month:** 17.00\n- **Gross monthly savings:** 408.00\n- **Monthly tooling cost:** 50.00\n- **Net monthly savings:** 358.00\n- **Implementation cost:** 6,000.00\n- **Payback (months):** 16.76\n- **ROI at 12 months:** -28 %\n\n**Assumptions**\n\n- Implementation cost: 6,000.00\n- Monthly tooling cost: 50.00\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-1>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-2>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-3>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-4>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-5>: 50 %\n- 1 step(s) have no expected reduction and count as zero savings\n\n## Risks\n\n- [RULES / DATA] Collect registration form handles sensitive data\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [RULES / DATA] Review signed contract handles sensitive data\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Review signed contract is business critical\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Decide credit limit is business critical\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Decide credit limit depends on human judgement\n- [AI / OPERATIONAL] Exceptions need an owner once the happy path is automated\n\n## Human controls\n\n- **Collect registration form:** REQUIRED. handles sensitive data; Reviewer decision: Reviewer keeps this step manual\n- **Review signed contract:** RECOMMENDED. handles sensitive data; high criticality\n- **Decide credit limit:** REQUIRED. requires human judgement; requires human approval\n\n## Workflow specification\n\n1. Trigger: a new process execution starts\n2. Collect registration form: MANUAL, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n3. Verify company registry and tax ID: RULE_BASED\n4. Review signed contract: AI_CANDIDATE, with a person reviewing a sample or the flagged cases\n5. Decide credit limit: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n6. Create customer in CRM and ERP: API_INTEGRATION\n7. Send welcome pack by post: MANUAL\n8. End: record the outcome and the time spent for later comparison\n",
